<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    repipe-68149b8a-stack-string-invalid-cast: "stack-string initialisation is
    emitted as an invalid array cast"
    docs/re-needs/stack-string-invalid-cast.md

    Source:   void f(void) { char buf[32] = "the quick brown fox jumped once";
                             customPrint(buf); }
    GCC -O2 copies the whole literal out of .rodata with two 128-bit
    movdqa/movaps pairs.  The wide loads survive as free read-only memory
    varnodes, so the copy reaches the printer as partial-symbol slice
    assignments - `v1._0_8_ = (char[8])msg._0_8_;` - which are not valid C (C
    has no array cast) and which hide the string the decompiler has already
    recovered at that address.

    Bytes compiled from that source on this machine (gcc -O2 -fno-pie), then
    linked with .text at 0x100000, .rodata at 0x101000 and customPrint at
    0x102000, so every RIP displacement is already resolved.

    Stage model: S5 const-sequence - the same sub-stage that owns
    RuleStringCopy (constant stack strings) and GH-9230 (constant-fill runs),
    here for a run whose SOURCE is read-only image memory rather than pcode
    constants.  The P0 assertion is `option rodatastring on|off`.

    Pass 1 (default): assertion #1 proves the recovered builtin_strncpy.
    Pass 2 (rodatastring off): assertion #2 reproduces the filed bug, the
    invalid array-typed cast.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
4883ec28660f6f05f40f00004889e70f
290424660f6f05f50f00000f29442410
e8db1f00004883c428c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x101000" readonly="true">
74686520717569636b2062726f776e20
666f78206a756d706564206f6e636500
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="f"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x102000" name="customPrint"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>parse line extern void f(void);</com>
  <com>parse line extern void customPrint(char *);</com>
  <com>map address r0x101000 char msg[32]</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option rodatastring off</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="rodatastring #1: default pipeline recovers the read-only block copy as one builtin_strncpy" min="1" max="1">builtin_strncpy\(v1,"the quick brown fox jumped once",0x20\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="rodatastring #2: rodatastring off restores the invalid array-typed cast (the filed bug)" min="1" max="1">v1\._0_8_ = \(char\[8\]\)msg\._0_8_;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
